# React Hooks Guide

Hooks let you use state and other React features without writing a class.

## useState

```jsx
import { useState } from 'react';

function Counter() {
    const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

    return (
        <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>
            Count: {count}
        </button>
    );
}
```

## useEffect

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
    document.title = `Count: ${count}`;
}, [count]);
```
